lue\": \"permitted\"}... no, skip. Keep it in description.\n\n- components: A/D conversion module, main board with processor — these are internal parts of the indicator, could be components[] entries with roles: \"analog-to-digital conversion module\", \"main board with processor\". The rule: components for named sub-assemblies. I'll include them:\n  - {role: \"A/D conversion module\", type_designations: []}\n  - {role: \"main board\", characteristics: {\"processor\": ...}} hmm. I'll do {role: \"main board with processor\", type_designations: []}. Maybe combine into description instead. I'll include minimal components entries.\n\nFunctions (zero setting, tare, etc.) — these are \"devices\"/functions; put into description or as characteristics list. I'll include in description.\n\nLoad cell requirements — description / recommendation R60 reference: \"Any compatible load cell with R60 OIML Certificate of Conformity\". This means the cert references R60. Should I add recommendation entry for R60? The recommendation layer is for the certificate's recommendation — which is R76. The R60 mention is a requirement for connected load cells, not the certificate's own recommendation. I'll mention in components/description. Maybe add to components: {role: \"load cell\", type_designations: [], alternatives: null, characteristics: {\"requirement\": {\"value\": \"R60 OIML Certificate of Conformity required\", \"unit_symbol\": null, \"unit_id\": null, \"footnote_markers\": []}}}. Hmm, characteristics{} in components is loosely defined. I could add:\n\ncomponents: [\n  {role: \"load cell\", type_designations: [], characteristics: {\"requirement\": {\"value\": \"R60 Certificate of Conformity\", \"unit_symbol\": null, \"unit_id\": null, \"footnote_markers\": []}}}\n]\n\nBut careful with structured values strictness — characteristics values must be the structured object shape. OK.\n\nActually rule 6 says record each named sub-assembly as components entry. The load cell is a generic connected device, not part of the certified type per se. The indicator is certified; platform and load cell are connected. I might record load cell as a component with the requirement noted. I think it's reasonable.\n\ntest_reports: [{id: \"P00917\", pages: 13, role: \"evaluation_report\"}]. Date unknown. role: \"type_evaluation_report\" or \"evaluation_report\"? The text says \"Evaluation Report P00917 (13 pages)\". I'll use \"evaluation_report\".\n\nrevision_history: not present. Omit.\n\nfootnotes: none present.\n\nmatrix_tables: none.\n\nmodel_level characteristics:\n1. enclosure_material: stainless steel / plastic per model.\n2. load_cell_connection: 4-wire / 6-wire per model.\n3. series: \"A\" / \"V\" per model — maybe attribute \"indicator_series\".\n\nValues as strings (allowed).\n\nAlso model_level entries structure: {\"attribute\", \"unit_symbol\", \"values\": [{\"model\", \"value\", \"unit_symbol\", \"unit_id\", \"footnote_markers\"}]}? The schema shows values: {model, value, footnote_markers[]}. Unit at attribute level for model_level (per example: unit_symbol at attribute level). For string values unit is null.\n\ntype_level characteristics:\n- accuracy_class: value \"III or IIII\" — or better captured in recommendation.accuracy_classes. I'll include in recommendation, and maybe type_level too. Keep recommendation only? Schema has recommendation.accuracy_classes. I'll put there: [\"III\", \"IIII\"].\n- power_supply: value \"mains or battery\" — string. Maybe power_supply_type with two entries? I'll do {\"power_supply\": {\"value\": \"mains or battery\", ...}}.\n- weighing_mode: \"self-indicating\"\n- weighing_intervals: \"single or dual interval/range\" → attribute \"intervals_ranges\": {value: \"single or dual\"}. \n- display: {\"value\": \"graphic LCD (2.0\\\" or 1.0\\\" depending on model)\"}.\n- direct_sales_to_public: {value: true}? I'll skip booleans; use description.\n\nLet me also include description summarizing functions and load cell requirements.\n\ncertificate:\n- number: \"R76/2006-GB1-12.10\"\n- page_total: 3\n- oiml_issuer_id: \"GB1\"\n- member_state: GB1 is the UK (Great Britain). Actually member state codes: GB = United Kingdom. \"GB1\" is the issuer ID. I'll omit member_state since not explicit, or set \"GB\"? The certificate number contains GB1 which is the UK issuing authority identifier. I think member_state: \"United Kingdom\" is a safe inference? Rule 8: don't fabricate. GB is a well-known code. Hmm. I'll include member_state: \"GB\" — actually, risk. I'll leave it out. Just oiml_issuer_id \"GB1\".\n\nissuing_authority: {oiml_issuer_id: \"GB1\"} — name unknown. Include? The layer exists; include with only oiml_issuer_id.\n\nDate issued: unknown (page 1 not available). Omit.\n\nscheme: For R76 certificate of the form R76/2006-GB1-12.10, this is a full type approval certificate of a NAUI/indicator... OIML-CS has Scheme A and B. Given 2006-era, scheme concept didn't exist; but extraction expects A or B. Not stated → omit.\n\nproject_number: unknown. Omit.\n\nLet me write the JSON.\n\nmodels:\nA-series: AFS, AFM, ABM, ATM, APS\nV-series: VFS, VFM, VBM, VTM, VPS\n\nWait — check: \"A-Series and V-Series digital indicators (AFS, AFM, ABM, ATM, APS, VFS, VFM, VBM, VTM, VPS models)\". Yes 5 A + 5 V.\n\nEnclosures: stainless steel: AFS, APS, VFS, VPS. Plastic: AFM, ATM, ABM, VFM, VBM, VTM.\n\nLoad cell connection: A-Series 4-wire, V-Series 6-wire.\n\nDisplay: 2.0\" or 1.0\" graphic LCD depending on model — mapping unknown, so keep type-level with combined string.\n\nmodel_level entries:\n\n[\n  {\"attribute\": \"indicator_series\", \"unit_symbol\": null, \"values\": [\n    {\"model\": \"AFS\", \"value\": \"A\"}, {\"model\": \"AFM\", \"value\": \"A\"}, {\"model\": \"ABM\", \"value\": \"A\"}, {\"model\": \"ATM\", \"value\": \"A\"}, {\"model\": \"APS\", \"value\": \"A\"},\n    {\"model\": \"VFS\", \"value\": \"V\"}, {\"model\": \"VFM\", \"value\": \"V\"}, {\"model\": \"VBM\", \"value\": \"V\"}, {\"model\": \"VTM\", \"value\": \"V\"}, {\"model\": \"VPS\", \"value\": \"V\"}\n  ]},\n  {\"attribute\": \"enclosure_material\", \"unit_symbol\": null, \"values\": [\n    {\"model\": \"AFS\", \"value\": \"stainless steel\"}, {\"model\": \"AFM\", \"value\": \"plastic\"}, {\"model\": \"ABM\", \"value\": \"plastic\"}, {\"model\": \"ATM\", \"value\": \"plastic\"}, {\"model\": \"APS\", \"value\": \"stainless steel\"},\n    {\"model\": \"VFS\", \"value\": \"stainless steel\"}, {\"model\": \"VFM\", \"value\": \"plastic\"}, {\"model\": \"VBM\", \"value\": \"plastic\"}, {\"model\": \"VTM\", \"value\": \"plastic\"}, {\"model\": \"VPS\", \"value\": \"stainless steel\"}\n  ]},\n  {\"attribute\": \"load_cell_connection\", \"unit_symbol\": null, \"values\": [\n    A-series: \"4-wire\" ×5, V-series: \"6-wire\" ×5\n  ]}\n]\n\ntype_level:\n- \"power_supply\": {\"value\": \"mains or battery\", \"unit_symbol\": null, \"unit_id\": null, \"footnote_markers\": []}\n- \"weighing_operation\": {\"value\": \"self-indicating\"}\n- \"intervals_ranges\": {\"value\": \"single or dual\"}\n- \"display\": {\"value\": \"graphic LCD, 2.0 inch or 1.0 inch depending on model\"}\n- \"accuracy_class\": {\"value\": \"III or IIII\"} — plus recommendation.accuracy_classes.\n- \"intended_use\": {\"value\": \"direct sales to the public\"}? Hmm, \"suitable for direct sales to the public\". I'll include \"direct_sales_to_public\": {\"value\": \"permitted\"}? I'd rather phrase value as string \"suitable for direct sales to the public\" under attribute \"intended_use\". Include.\n\nFunctions → description.\n\ncomponents:\n- {role: \"A/D conversion module\", type_designations: []}\n- {role: \"main board with processor\", type_designations: []}\n- {role: \"load cell (connected)\", type_designations: [], characteristics: {\"requirement\": {\"value\": \"R60 OIML Certificate of Conformity required; compatibility of modules data required; NH-marked cells permitted only with R76 humidity testing\"}}}\n\nHmm — components characterist